course: dictionary
lesson: 11229
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «The woolly hat kept her warm on the frosty walk.» Here woolly means made of wool, soft and warm.
explain: «The woolly mammoth had thick hair to survive the Ice Age.» Now woolly describes an animal with long, thick, soft hair like wool. The clues are mammoth, hair and the cold, so the meaning is about hair, not about a hat.
explain: «Her answer was too woolly; the teacher wanted exact facts.» Here woolly means vague and muddled, not clear. A good check is to swap in a meaning. Does «vague» fit? Yes, so that is the meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: One word can have several meanings, and context shows you which one is used.
fact: «Woolly» can mean made of wool, having thick soft hair, or vague and not clear.
fact: A «woolly mammoth» was an animal that lived during the last Ice Age, long after the dinosaurs.
fact: A «toque» is a Canadian word for a woolly hat.
exercise: «Mia pulled on her woolly hat before going out in the snow.» What does woolly mean here? | Muddled and unclear | *Made of wool, soft and warm | Very old | Wet and slippery
exercise: «The woolly mammoth had thick hair to survive the Ice Age.» What does woolly describe here? | A hard, shiny stone | *An animal with thick, soft hair like wool | A thin, cold river | Angry and loud
exercise: Mr Hale says, «Your answer is woolly; give me exact facts.» What does woolly mean? | *Vague and muddled | Clear and exact | Made of wool | Quick and loud
test: Jenna wrote «woolly ideas» in her essay. What does woolly mean in her essay? | Long and thick | Warm and cosy | *Vague and not clear | Made of wool
test: Which phrase uses woolly to mean made of wool? | Woolly answers | Woolly mammoth | Woolly thinking | *Woolly socks
exam: Connor asks what a «toque» is. What is the answer? | A type of boat | A word for a child | *A woolly hat | A coffee with two creams and two sugars
